# Sensitive-data patterns for tools/check-secrets.py and
# tools/scrub.py.
#
# Each non-comment line is either:
#
#   PATTERN                  (a literal string to detect; flagged
#                             by check-secrets.py and replaced with
#                             a generic placeholder by scrub.py)
#
#   PATTERN  ->  REPLACEMENT (detect AND replace; useful when
#                             you want the cleanup to swap the
#                             leak for a specific placeholder)
#
# This file is committed. Copy it to ``tools/secrets.txt`` and
# add your real specifics there (``tools/secrets.txt`` is
# gitignored). Then run:
#
#   python3 tools/check-secrets.py all

# --- Examples (uncomment + edit; do not commit real values) ---
# /home/<your-user>/<app>            -> /home/user/<app>
# conda activate <your-env-name>      -> conda activate <env>
# AAaa<your-password>                 -> <REDACTED-PASSWORD>
